      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(e2e): bound Docker stats sample lines",
        "body": "AI-assisted: yes (Codex)\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Docker E2E resource-ceiling checks could keep accumulating an oversized stats JSONL sample line before rejecting it, letting a malformed or stalled stats writer consume unnecessary memory.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe stats scanner now counts streamed sample-line bytes and rejects any single sample line over 1 MiB before JSON parsing. Normal newline-delimited Docker stats samples still stream through the same resource ceiling checks, including LF, CRLF, and standalone CR delimiters.\n\n## User Impact\n\nE2E resource checks fail fast on oversized Docker stats samples while continuing to accept valid bounded samples.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent head: 9a5fdd8a106d94c87d7cfa9d76b782eaa2ff4a3a\n\n- Real Docker stats resource-ceiling CLI proof passed: node scripts/e2e/lib/docker-stats/assert-resource-ceiling.mjs <valid Docker stats JSONL> 256.5 50.5 proof-valid printed \"proof-valid resource peak: memory=128.0MiB cpu=25.0% samples=1\".\n- Oversized-line proof passed: the same CLI with a single Docker stats JSONL sample over 1 MiB exited non-zero with \"exceeded 1048576 bytes\" and did not report \"was not valid JSON\", showing the line cap fires before JSON parsing.\n- git diff --check passed.\n- Exact-head GitHub checks after rebase passed for Real behavior proof, check-test-types, and openclaw/ci-gate on 9a5fdd8a106d94c87d7cfa9d76b782eaa2ff4a3a.\n",
        "branch": "qingminglong/docker-stats-line-cap",
